Lobster_Lord said:
I have messed around with some AI-generated stuff
Click to expand...
But have you simply Googled it?
I typed in "rpg maker mv picture hover" and got about half a dozen threads from here and Reddit pertinent to the question, plus a YouTube video tutorial.
Some of them are only for events, and some are for MZ, but - for example, there was an event script posted by
@caethyril
that did exactly what you were asking for MZ, so you could easily have asked her if it needed adaptation to work in MZ, and how.
It just seems like spending time getting information from people who actually know things would be a better first choice than breaking your game with computers making up code.
In any case, paste the below into a text editor, save as a *.js file, and include as a plugin
Code:
TouchInput._onMouseMove = function(event) 
{
    if (this._mousePressed) {
        var x = Graphics.pageToCanvasX(event.pageX);
        var y = Graphics.pageToCanvasY(event.pageY);
        this._onMove(x, y);
    }
    this.hoverX = Graphics.pageToCanvasX(event.pageX);
    this.hoverY = Graphics.pageToCanvasY(event.pageY);
};
Then you can check at any time the variables
TouchInput.hoverX
and
TouchInput.hoverY
to get the current coordinates of the cursor.
So you could do a parallel event on your map looking like this:
You use conditional branches to see if the cursor is within the area of the picture; if yes, and it hasn't already been made opaque, do so.
If it is outside of the picture's area, and it hasn't been made transparent again, do so.
You can can probably put a few frames of Wait at the bottom just so it isn't running every single frame without it looking delayed.
